WEBVTT

00:00:04.770 --> 00:00:07.070
The new school year starts today.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:09.920
My uniform I sent out for cleaning is sparkling.

00:00:09.920 --> 00:00:10.990
My shoes are sparkling, too.

00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:14.840
Alice, you're like a sparkling first year.

00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:15.990
I'm a second year.

00:00:21.380 --> 00:00:24.000
Look at how brightly the world is shining.

00:00:25.430 --> 00:00:27.000
It really is.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.510
Good mornin'!

00:00:46.470 --> 00:00:50.900
We always take this route, but it seems a little brighter today.

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:54.900
I'm so excited for all the new things in the new year.

00:00:55.280 --> 00:00:56.610
Me, too!

00:00:57.570 --> 00:01:00.790
Yes... And we'll be in new classes, too.

00:01:01.090 --> 00:01:02.450
You're not shining!

00:01:02.450 --> 00:01:04.290
She's been like this all morning.

00:01:04.290 --> 00:01:05.540
What's wrong?

00:01:07.380 --> 00:01:09.810
I envy your optimism.

00:01:09.810 --> 00:01:13.010
When I think we might be split up...

00:01:13.010 --> 00:01:14.050
Split up?

00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:17.560
This sky is connected wherever we go.

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:20.970
Not even national borders can separate us.

00:01:28.650 --> 00:01:30.980
Looks like it's a classroom wall separating us.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:04.990
Karen!

00:03:05.450 --> 00:03:06.990
We're in the same class.

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.670
Shino!

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:11.500
I'm so happy we're in the same class!

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:16.670
<i>Gloom...</i>

00:03:16.670 --> 00:03:17.760
Aya-chan?

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:20.010
It seems being separated from Youko was quite a shock.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:24.050
<i>Gloom...</i>

00:03:24.050 --> 00:03:25.230
I know.

00:03:25.230 --> 00:03:27.010
You wanted to be with Shino, right?

00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.960
Shino isn't in this class.

00:03:31.960 --> 00:03:33.020
What should I do?

00:03:33.020 --> 00:03:34.650
There's nothing you can do.

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:38.470
Hey, you don't look well.

00:03:38.470 --> 00:03:40.150
Do you want to go rest in the nurse's office?

00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:41.450
You're right.

00:03:42.530 --> 00:03:44.780
I'm going to lie down.

00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.030
Get a grip!

00:03:47.620 --> 00:03:48.910
Alice.

00:03:48.910 --> 00:03:51.490
Youko, we came to play.

00:03:51.490 --> 00:03:52.790
Excuse us.

00:03:54.000 --> 00:03:55.490
Perfect timing.

00:03:55.490 --> 00:03:56.540
Alice isn't doing so well.

00:03:59.050 --> 00:04:00.460
Shino!

00:04:02.440 --> 00:04:06.480
Shino, Shino, Shino!

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:10.250
I'm fine!

00:04:13.480 --> 00:04:16.310
It's hard to believe you were shining so brightly this morning.

00:04:16.310 --> 00:04:19.230
Our classrooms are just a little further away.

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:20.800
It's not just a little!

00:04:20.800 --> 00:04:22.150
It's the distance between Japan...

00:04:22.150 --> 00:04:24.230
...and England!

00:04:24.840 --> 00:04:25.910
Alice...

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:26.930
Aya...

00:04:27.510 --> 00:04:29.950
You've never had so much in common before.

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:31.870
You're exaggerating.

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.790
You two seem more flippant than usual.

00:04:37.790 --> 00:04:38.710
That's right.

00:04:39.300 --> 00:04:40.840
Flippant?

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.590
This is how we always are.

00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:43.220
Right?

00:04:43.220 --> 00:04:44.220
Yes.

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.970
See?

00:04:49.970 --> 00:04:52.600
You're 30% more flippant than usual!

00:04:52.600 --> 00:04:54.980
I can't believe how difficult they're being.

00:04:55.850 --> 00:04:58.310
I understand why Alice is sad,

00:04:58.310 --> 00:05:00.270
but you've got two friends in your class, Aya.

00:05:00.270 --> 00:05:01.110
That's not bad.

00:05:02.990 --> 00:05:06.320
Youko, you're not sad we're separated?

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:07.820
Well, I've got Alice.

00:05:08.790 --> 00:05:10.740
That's not fair!

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:13.500
Ayaya!

00:05:13.890 --> 00:05:16.500
Did she want to be in Alice's class that badly?

00:05:18.750 --> 00:05:21.940
Good morning, everyone.

00:05:21.940 --> 00:05:23.260
As we welcome our new first years,

00:05:23.260 --> 00:05:26.590
the new school year is finally beginning.

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:31.260
<i>She really wanted to be in the same class as Oomiya-san.</i>

00:05:32.470 --> 00:05:36.980
<i>They say rabbits die of loneliness, but I wonder if it's true.</i>

00:05:43.650 --> 00:05:45.030
Alice-san!

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:48.030
I'm your homeroom teacher again!

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.660
You can ask me for anything!

00:05:51.580 --> 00:05:52.280
Later.

00:05:52.280 --> 00:05:53.240
Okay.

00:05:55.160 --> 00:05:57.790
Youko, what were you talking about?

00:05:58.290 --> 00:06:00.970
She asked me to give you her regards.

00:06:00.970 --> 00:06:02.550
Best regards.

00:06:02.550 --> 00:06:03.880
Regards.

00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:12.680
<i>It's like Niagara Falls...</i>

00:06:12.680 --> 00:06:13.150
Hey.

00:06:13.150 --> 00:06:13.960
Ouch.

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:18.390
Karen, why is your hair so beautiful?

00:06:18.390 --> 00:06:19.900
Is it?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.360
You and Ayaya have similar hair.

00:06:22.720 --> 00:06:24.730
You mean since it's straight?

00:06:25.530 --> 00:06:28.650
Maybe they divided us based on our hair type!

00:06:28.650 --> 00:06:29.860
I see.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:38.410
<i>Unlike me, you have fluffy dog hair.</i>

00:06:38.410 --> 00:06:39.870
She's still mad!

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.960
Do you want to go hang out with Shino and the others?

00:06:45.590 --> 00:06:47.810
No, I'm okay.

00:06:47.810 --> 00:06:49.800
Sorry for making you worry.

00:06:49.800 --> 00:06:52.390
I'm glad we're in the same class.

00:06:52.790 --> 00:06:53.800
Really?

00:06:53.800 --> 00:06:54.920
<i>That's good.</i>

00:06:54.920 --> 00:06:56.970
<i>She seems to be feeling better.</i>

00:06:56.970 --> 00:06:58.230
I look forward to being in class with you.

00:06:58.550 --> 00:07:00.480
Yeah, me too.

00:07:02.770 --> 00:07:05.690
<i>The damage is even worse than I thought.</i>

00:07:05.690 --> 00:07:07.740
Are you fine without Karen?

00:07:08.240 --> 00:07:12.240
That would mean two blondes in one class.

00:07:12.240 --> 00:07:14.120
That would really make the class shine.

00:07:16.370 --> 00:07:18.120
Sparkle, sparkle!

00:07:18.620 --> 00:07:21.830
Maybe they don't put foreign students in the same class.

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:24.000
Maybe it's better that way.

00:07:24.420 --> 00:07:25.500
Stand.

00:07:25.820 --> 00:07:26.500
Bow.

00:07:26.500 --> 00:07:28.010
Good bye.

00:07:28.010 --> 00:07:29.010
Shino, let's go home!

00:07:29.010 --> 00:07:30.170
That was quick!

00:07:34.760 --> 00:07:38.650
We only had the opening ceremony today, but it felt so long.

00:07:39.640 --> 00:07:40.730
You're right.

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:43.420
It'll be all right, you two.

00:07:43.420 --> 00:07:45.520
Remember our first year?

00:07:45.940 --> 00:07:50.280
I was in a different class from everyone else, but I wasn't lonely at all.

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:54.800
Now that you mention it, you were in a different class.

00:07:54.800 --> 00:07:57.160
You were always coming to ours.

00:07:57.160 --> 00:07:58.660
I'm finished.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.910
I'm going to take this to the faculty office.

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:03.170
I'll go with you.

00:08:05.670 --> 00:08:08.210
How is your new class?

00:08:08.210 --> 00:08:10.880
Karasuma-sensei is your homeroom teacher, isn't she?

00:08:10.880 --> 00:08:13.050
I'm so jealous.

00:08:13.050 --> 00:08:15.680
Class A's homeroom teacher is wonderful, too.

00:08:17.550 --> 00:08:20.060
Shino, you don't seem too lonely.

00:08:20.470 --> 00:08:21.230
What?

00:08:23.740 --> 00:08:27.560
Well, you came all the way across the ocean.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:31.560
Compared to that, this is nothing.

00:08:31.560 --> 00:08:33.570
You're just a classroom away.

00:08:36.200 --> 00:08:37.320
Yeah...

00:08:37.870 --> 00:08:41.580
Yeah, you're right.

00:08:54.430 --> 00:08:55.720
Good morning.

00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.390
Good morning, Alice-chan.

00:08:58.680 --> 00:09:00.850
Come on, Isami.

00:09:00.850 --> 00:09:02.200
Go to university.

00:09:43.720 --> 00:09:44.930
Good morning.

00:09:45.290 --> 00:09:46.810
Good mornin'!

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:48.730
The weather is nice.

00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:50.810
Sunny days make me feel so energetic!

00:09:51.230 --> 00:09:54.530
Karen, you're full of energy on rainy and cloudy days, too.

00:09:57.700 --> 00:10:00.070
I wonder if anything fun will happen today.

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:05.160
<i>A year ago, I came to Japan because I wanted to see Shino.</i>

00:10:05.160 --> 00:10:08.710
<i>Just like I resolved to come across the ocean...</i>

00:10:08.710 --> 00:10:11.590
<i>I just have to cross over to the next classroom.</i>

00:10:12.840 --> 00:10:16.740
Sensei, can I attend class with Class A today?

00:10:16.740 --> 00:10:18.970
No way!

00:10:28.700 --> 00:10:32.360
The protagonist of this manga is so cool.

00:10:33.860 --> 00:10:35.780
I told you, there is nothing wrong.

00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:38.070
Thanks for waiting!

00:10:38.070 --> 00:10:38.860
You're late.

00:10:39.320 --> 00:10:40.830
What happened to you?!

00:10:40.830 --> 00:10:42.660
Is that a back scratcher?!

00:10:43.030 --> 00:10:44.540
Good mornin'!

00:10:44.540 --> 00:10:45.950
Good morning, Karen.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:47.330
Good morning.

00:10:47.330 --> 00:10:48.540
G-Good morning.

00:10:48.540 --> 00:10:49.940
Good morning.

00:10:49.940 --> 00:10:51.800
Uh, do you have a sty?

00:10:53.040 --> 00:10:58.050
When my left eye tingles, the world will meet its demise.

00:10:59.220 --> 00:11:00.220
Huh?

00:11:00.220 --> 00:11:02.010
That's so cool.

00:11:03.760 --> 00:11:06.060
Karen, save that for later!

00:11:09.480 --> 00:11:11.560
This is what they call middle school fantasies.

00:11:11.560 --> 00:11:13.270
We're high school first years, though.

00:11:13.270 --> 00:11:14.570
This too?

00:11:15.070 --> 00:11:16.570
You're taking this pretty far!

00:11:16.570 --> 00:11:19.030
Oh, I got this when I tripped yesterday.

00:11:19.030 --> 00:11:20.450
Don't be so misleading!

00:11:22.420 --> 00:11:24.280
You were inspired by a manga?

00:11:24.280 --> 00:11:28.290
This character has divine powers in his left eye.

00:11:28.290 --> 00:11:29.140
Yeah?

00:11:29.140 --> 00:11:30.790
What's the point of the eyepatch?

00:11:30.790 --> 00:11:33.420
I haven't read that part yet.

00:11:33.420 --> 00:11:35.340
I'm still in the middle of the first volume.

00:11:35.340 --> 00:11:36.300
You got obsessed quick!

00:11:36.880 --> 00:11:40.510
I understand what it's like to be inspired by stories.

00:11:40.510 --> 00:11:43.090
I've been reading some classics lately.

00:11:43.090 --> 00:11:45.300
You're reading some difficult books.

00:11:45.760 --> 00:11:47.600
I thought I might learn something.

00:11:47.600 --> 00:11:50.270
I look up words as I read, so my shoulders get stiff.

00:11:50.270 --> 00:11:52.440
Sometimes I massage her shoulders.

00:11:52.860 --> 00:11:53.980
Like this.

00:11:53.980 --> 00:11:55.900
Miss, your shoulders are so stiff.

00:11:55.900 --> 00:11:57.940
Yes, right there.

00:11:58.900 --> 00:12:00.490
Oh, I know.

00:12:00.490 --> 00:12:02.360
In order to ease the burden on your sloping shoulders,

00:12:02.360 --> 00:12:04.450
I will read aloud to you.

00:12:04.450 --> 00:12:06.070
My shoulders aren't sloped.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:08.410
Let's see.

00:12:09.040 --> 00:12:10.870
This is difficult, isn't it?

00:12:10.870 --> 00:12:12.460
It's like some kind of code.

00:12:12.890 --> 00:12:15.080
My shoulders are starting to get stiff.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:17.460
Shino, you haven't read a single line!

00:12:18.110 --> 00:12:20.160
My eyelids are starting to droop, too.

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:21.760
Could it be?

00:12:22.110 --> 00:12:24.050
A cursed book!

00:12:24.050 --> 00:12:25.760
Don't bond over that.

00:12:25.760 --> 00:12:28.930
Maybe you could come up with a story to read together.

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:29.940
I see.

00:12:29.940 --> 00:12:30.930
That might work.

00:12:32.830 --> 00:12:35.980
But I've never written a story before.

00:12:36.520 --> 00:12:39.110
As long as you have an active imagination, you'll be fine.

00:12:39.110 --> 00:12:40.480
For example...

00:12:41.110 --> 00:12:44.840
Once upon a time, there was an old woman.

00:12:44.840 --> 00:12:46.280
You're so mean!

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:48.780
I never said you were the model for the old lady!

00:12:48.780 --> 00:12:50.290
What an impressive imagination.

00:12:50.700 --> 00:12:53.080
The old woman went to the river to wash her clothes.

00:12:53.080 --> 00:12:54.620
Oh, Momotaro.

00:12:54.620 --> 00:12:56.580
That's just an old folk tale.

00:12:56.580 --> 00:12:58.290
No, Youko.

00:12:58.290 --> 00:13:00.000
You need to fantasise more.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:00.880
Fantasise?!

00:13:01.300 --> 00:13:03.970
Fantasise about people you know.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:05.590
You can make me the hero!

00:13:05.590 --> 00:13:07.760
I think that might actually be harder.

00:13:07.760 --> 00:13:11.770
You're definitely the type to tear down a city, Karen.

00:13:15.980 --> 00:13:17.150
Aya?

00:13:17.150 --> 00:13:18.150
No!

00:13:18.150 --> 00:13:20.440
Stop, thoughts!

00:13:20.440 --> 00:13:21.780
What kind of fantasy are you having?

00:13:23.360 --> 00:13:26.780
Knowing you, I bet it was about a prince on a white horse.

00:13:27.240 --> 00:13:28.620
It was not!

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:29.320
It was a donkey.

00:13:29.320 --> 00:13:30.200
A brown one.

00:13:30.200 --> 00:13:30.910
A donkey?

00:13:31.410 --> 00:13:33.750
A white horse wouldn't suit you.

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:35.000
It was about me?

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:38.380
I-It's Karen's fault for telling us to use people we know!

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:39.580
I don't mind.

00:13:39.580 --> 00:13:41.460
You idiot!

00:13:42.410 --> 00:13:44.590
Fantasise, huh?

00:13:45.170 --> 00:13:46.440
Did you know?

00:13:46.440 --> 00:13:48.760
Alice is a robot I made.

00:13:48.760 --> 00:13:50.070
What?!

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:51.470
That's interesting.

00:13:51.470 --> 00:13:53.220
It's true.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:56.350
To prove it, there's a switch on her back.

00:14:04.280 --> 00:14:08.450
Shino, you looked so serious, everyone believed you!

00:14:10.450 --> 00:14:12.280
If I don't come up with a story,

00:14:12.280 --> 00:14:14.790
I won't be able to put Alice to sleep tonight.

00:14:14.790 --> 00:14:16.320
What are you talking about?

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:20.590
I thought of something.

00:14:20.590 --> 00:14:21.630
Really?

00:14:21.630 --> 00:14:22.960
What kind of story is it?

00:14:23.460 --> 00:14:28.030
There were two blonde princesses living in a certain place.

00:14:28.030 --> 00:14:30.470
The models for the princesses are me and Alice.

00:14:32.300 --> 00:14:33.950
Shino, what about me?

00:14:33.950 --> 00:14:34.720
What about me?

00:14:35.080 --> 00:14:36.390
Just wait.

00:14:36.390 --> 00:14:38.290
I'll get to it.

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:42.320
Now, then...

00:14:43.290 --> 00:14:47.360
The two girls had been good friends since they were children.

00:14:57.590 --> 00:14:59.870
It's done.

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.290
Thank you, Shino.

00:15:01.650 --> 00:15:03.060
Let's go for a walk.

00:15:11.340 --> 00:15:15.970
You really do like blonde hair, don't you, Shino?

00:15:16.310 --> 00:15:18.390
Yes, it's my treasure.

00:15:18.390 --> 00:15:25.480
What is your treasure, Alice?

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:26.270
You!

00:15:30.690 --> 00:15:32.200
Pirates?

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:40.080
My name is Captain Karen.

00:15:40.080 --> 00:15:43.880
Hand over your treasure.

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:47.500
But I don't have anything valuable.

00:15:49.760 --> 00:15:51.470
What is your treasure?

00:15:51.470 --> 00:15:53.180
Blonde hair.

00:15:53.180 --> 00:15:54.800
What is your treasure?

00:15:54.800 --> 00:15:55.800
Shino!

00:16:00.580 --> 00:16:04.310
Men, set sail!

00:16:04.930 --> 00:16:07.020
Shino, Shino.

00:16:07.020 --> 00:16:10.460
Shino!

00:16:10.460 --> 00:16:12.530
Shino...

00:16:12.530 --> 00:16:14.210
Alice.

00:16:14.210 --> 00:16:16.660
Don't cry during your own story.

00:16:16.660 --> 00:16:18.790
What's going to happen to Shino?

00:16:18.790 --> 00:16:20.540
Is she going to disappear at sea?

00:16:20.540 --> 00:16:22.710
That's too much of a bad ending.

00:16:26.590 --> 00:16:28.040
Why did you take me?

00:16:28.500 --> 00:16:32.380
If you want treasure, I'm sure you could find plenty somewhere else...

00:16:32.380 --> 00:16:33.630
It will be mine.

00:16:33.970 --> 00:16:35.970
It will all be mine.

00:16:35.970 --> 00:16:38.470
That is no fun.

00:16:38.470 --> 00:16:43.190
I have travelled the world.

00:16:43.190 --> 00:16:44.980
Gold, silver, treasure.

00:16:44.980 --> 00:16:46.400
Every day full of excitement.

00:16:46.400 --> 00:16:51.690
But I am excited by these things no longer.

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:59.730
We are the pirates who rule the seven seas.

00:17:01.040 --> 00:17:08.250
I found the ends of the world.

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.030
There is no end.

00:17:10.030 --> 00:17:11.670
The world is round.

00:17:12.030 --> 00:17:13.170
I read it in a book.

00:17:13.550 --> 00:17:14.670
But that's just a book.

00:17:14.670 --> 00:17:17.090
Why don't you go see for yourself?

00:17:17.090 --> 00:17:24.430
I'm sure you'll find a world you've never seen before.

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:27.900
Maybe I can find it if I'm with you.

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:31.610
As long as I'm with you.

00:17:31.610 --> 00:17:33.760
You can call me Shino.

00:17:33.760 --> 00:17:34.780
Shino...

00:17:34.780 --> 00:17:36.950
Shino, Shino, Shino!

00:17:37.910 --> 00:17:42.790
Let's sail the seas together.

00:17:43.250 --> 00:17:49.210
But first, may I write a letter to my friend?

00:17:49.210 --> 00:17:50.880
Shino.

00:17:50.880 --> 00:17:55.010
Why does it feel like she's speaking right to my soul?

00:17:55.010 --> 00:17:56.590
Her story is drawing me in.

00:17:56.590 --> 00:17:59.680
What would the two of you like to be?

00:17:59.680 --> 00:18:00.850
We're in the story?

00:18:02.510 --> 00:18:03.930
I guess Aya would be a mermaid.

00:18:03.930 --> 00:18:04.640
What?

00:18:04.640 --> 00:18:06.520
Youko would be a prince.

00:18:06.520 --> 00:18:07.390
What?

00:18:07.390 --> 00:18:09.270
Yeah, that's perfect.

00:18:09.270 --> 00:18:11.710
Let's go with that, then.

00:18:11.710 --> 00:18:12.760
Ahem.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:17.150
Karen's pirate ship was capsized in a storm.

00:18:18.110 --> 00:18:21.280
No!

00:18:29.540 --> 00:18:30.920
Where am I?

00:18:32.400 --> 00:18:34.420
I can't touch the bottom.

00:18:34.730 --> 00:18:35.890
It's all right.

00:18:35.890 --> 00:18:37.420
Hold on tight.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:41.390
That ship...

00:18:43.010 --> 00:18:50.100
I have always longed to see you again.

00:18:50.900 --> 00:18:54.730
I feel like I can touch you if I reach my hand out.

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:56.530
But it's all right.

00:18:56.530 --> 00:19:04.020
Just watching you from here is enough.

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:06.200
You really like her.

00:19:06.200 --> 00:19:08.290
She was just on my mind a little.

00:19:08.750 --> 00:19:13.210
Are you the one who saved me when I was shipwrecked?

00:19:13.210 --> 00:19:13.880
You are, aren't you?

00:19:13.880 --> 00:19:15.420
You're wrong.

00:19:15.750 --> 00:19:17.510
I've thought of you all this time.

00:19:17.510 --> 00:19:20.630
I've always wanted to see you again.

00:19:23.550 --> 00:19:25.970
Give Shino back!

00:19:25.970 --> 00:19:27.350
Karen.

00:19:27.350 --> 00:19:29.100
There you are, pirate.

00:19:29.100 --> 00:19:29.980
Fire!

00:19:30.340 --> 00:19:31.310
Yes!

00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:33.310
Ready the cannons!

00:19:51.540 --> 00:19:52.710
Karen...

00:19:52.710 --> 00:19:55.340
You're mistaken, Karen!

00:19:55.340 --> 00:19:56.880
You can't stop them now.

00:19:56.880 --> 00:19:58.210
Why not?

00:19:58.210 --> 00:20:01.470
What can we do?

00:20:13.730 --> 00:20:15.980
Humans are such fools.

00:20:16.730 --> 00:20:18.400
The Witch of the Depths.

00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:21.860
Witch-oneechan, I want to stop their fighting.

00:20:22.450 --> 00:20:23.680
Very well.

00:20:23.680 --> 00:20:25.490
I'll grant anything you wish.

00:20:26.070 --> 00:20:30.160
However, I'll only do it in exchange for something you treasure.

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:33.160
My treasure...

00:20:34.940 --> 00:20:37.750
Aya-chan, do you have any scissors?

00:20:37.750 --> 00:20:38.900
What?

00:20:38.900 --> 00:20:39.750
Yes.

00:20:40.350 --> 00:20:43.880
If you don't hurry up, they'll all be gone.

00:20:44.840 --> 00:20:46.610
Shino.

00:20:46.610 --> 00:20:47.550
Alice.

00:20:51.560 --> 00:20:53.060
I give this to you.

00:20:53.060 --> 00:21:01.420
Please stop their fighting!

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:06.870
And so, the princess lost her golden hair,

00:21:06.870 --> 00:21:10.090
and peace prevailed throughout the world.

00:21:14.580 --> 00:21:15.910
The end.

00:21:18.250 --> 00:21:19.170
Shino.

00:21:19.170 --> 00:21:21.500
It was all thanks to you, Shino.

00:21:21.500 --> 00:21:22.550
Shino.

00:21:22.550 --> 00:21:24.130
You did it for us.

00:21:24.130 --> 00:21:25.820
It was just a story.

00:21:25.820 --> 00:21:27.180
Shino didn't do anything.

00:21:27.180 --> 00:21:28.140
What's going on?

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:42.150
The top is a pole, and the bottom is... Oh?

00:21:42.780 --> 00:21:45.150
Please let me through.

00:21:46.030 --> 00:21:47.910
We're going to begin our morning announcements.

00:21:48.410 --> 00:21:51.660
Please return to your own classrooms.

00:21:53.910 --> 00:21:58.000
Shino, were the two princesses separated forever?

00:21:58.750 --> 00:22:00.590
Of course not.

00:22:00.590 --> 00:22:04.140
They can see each other any time, and they'll always be friends.

00:22:04.140 --> 00:22:05.340
Just like us.

00:22:07.640 --> 00:22:10.850
In this age, it's just a short flight on a plane.

00:22:10.850 --> 00:22:11.580
What?

00:22:11.580 --> 00:22:13.220
That story took place in modern day?

00:22:14.470 --> 00:22:16.290
Who knows?

00:22:31.620 --> 00:22:32.850
Japan.

00:22:40.710 --> 00:22:42.750
School.

00:22:52.570 --> 00:22:53.660
Hello.

00:22:57.890 --> 00:23:00.140
This letter was the start of it all.

00:23:00.140 --> 00:23:01.690
You're right.

00:23:02.520 --> 00:23:04.860
Shinobu, Alice-chan.

00:23:04.860 --> 00:23:06.110
Yes.

00:23:06.820 --> 00:23:07.740
Let's go.

00:23:07.740 --> 00:23:08.440
Yeah.

00:23:08.440 --> 00:23:10.520
Youko and the others might already be waiting for us.
